-- Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 (Cth)
-- Print: first reading (Senate), presented and read a first time on 7 September 2026
-- (Senator Payman; Parliament's file 26S2721; source bundle item bill-26S2721).
-- Part 1 -- Preliminary: Division 1 (ss 1-5) and Division 2 (ss 6-8).
--
-- Encoded in the Bill's own terms. Every rule quotes its provision and carries an @ref.
-- Where the text supports two readings that change an outcome, the reading taken is the plain
-- rule and the other is a rule whose name ends ", reading B"; registers/fork-register.json
-- says which and why, and cases.l4 asserts both on the facts that divide them.
-- Questions the encoding forced, and choices made, are in ENCODING-NOTES.md (E-nn).
-- Not encoded as rules (coverage.json, not_encoded): s 3 (simplified outline), column 3 of the
-- s 2(1) table, the notes, the table of contents and the long title.

IMPORT `aia-time`
IMPORT `mops-1984`

§ `Facts about the world the Bill reads`

-- The Bill takes these as facts: when the Royal Assent was given (s 2), the public holidays and
-- office closures that s 36(2) of the Acts Interpretation Act extends a deadline over, and the
-- days each House actually sat (s 9(5), read with s 2M of that Act). Day numbers throughout.
DECLARE World HAS
    `the day of the Royal Assent`         IS A NUMBER
    `holidays`                            IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `Senate sitting days`                 IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `House of Representatives sitting days` IS A LIST OF NUMBER

§ `Division 1 -- Preliminary`

§§ `1 Short title`

-- s 1: "This Act is the Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Act 2026."
@ref s 1
`the short title` MEANS "Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Act 2026"

§§ `2 Commencement`

-- s 2(1): "Each provision of this Act specified in column 1 of the table commences, or is taken to
-- have commenced, in accordance with column 2 of the table." Table item 1: "The whole of this
-- Act | The day after this Act receives the Royal Assent."
-- Acts Interpretation Act s 3: a provision expressed to commence on a day comes into operation at
-- the start of that day; s 3A does not apply because the Bill provides for its commencement
-- (s 3A(1)).
-- s 2(2) (column 3 is not part of the Act) and the note to s 2(1) are not encoded.
@ref s 2(1), table item 1; Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 3
GIVEN w IS A World
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day this Act commences` w MEANS
    `the moment of operation of an Act expressed to commence on` (w's `the day of the Royal Assent` PLUS 1)

-- s 3 (Simplified outline) is not encoded as a rule: see coverage.json.

§§ `4 Application of this Act`

DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `in Australia`
    `in an external Territory`
    `outside Australia`

-- s 4: "This Act applies both within and outside Australia and extends to every external
-- Territory."
@ref s 4
GIVEN p IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act applies` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `in Australia` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in an external Territory` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `outside Australia` THEN TRUE

§§ `5 Crown to be bound`

DECLARE Crown IS ONE OF
    `the Crown in right of the Commonwealth`
    `the Crown in right of a State`
    `the Crown in right of the Australian Capital Territory`
    `the Crown in right of the Northern Territory`

-- s 5: "This Act binds the Crown in right of the Commonwealth. However, it does not bind the
-- Crown in right of a State, of the Australian Capital Territory or of the Northern Territory."
@ref s 5
GIVEN c IS A Crown
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act binds` c IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Crown in right of the Commonwealth` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§ `Division 2 -- Definitions and key concepts`

§§ `6 Definitions`

-- s 6: "Minister means the Minister administering the Diplomatic and Consular Missions Act 1978."
-- Who that is on a given day is a fact (reference register REF-04: the Administrative
-- Arrangements Order and the Acts Interpretation Act s 19).
@ref s 6 'Minister'
GIVEN `administers the Diplomatic and Consular Missions Act 1978` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Minister` `administers the Diplomatic and Consular Missions Act 1978` IF
    `administers the Diplomatic and Consular Missions Act 1978`

-- s 6: "Secretary means the Secretary of the Department administered by the Minister."
-- No operative provision of the Bill uses the term (ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-09).
@ref s 6 'Secretary'
GIVEN `is Secretary of the Department the Minister administers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Secretary` `is Secretary of the Department the Minister administers` IF
    `is Secretary of the Department the Minister administers`

-- s 6: "designated diplomatic office: see section 7." "disqualifying political affiliation: see
-- subsection 8(1)." "Selection Committee: see subsection 12(2)." "significant political
-- affiliation: see subsection 8(2)." "rules means rules made under section 16." These signpost
-- definitions are encoded where the defined term bites: s 7, s 8, s 12 (part3) and s 16 (part4).

§§ `7 What is a designated diplomatic office?`

DECLARE Office IS ONE OF
    `Ambassador to the United States of America`
    `Consul-General in the United States of America` HAS `post` IS A STRING
    `High Commissioner to the United Kingdom`
    `High Commissioner to New Zealand`
    `Ambassador to Ireland`
    `Ambassador to the Netherlands`
    `High Commissioner to India`
    `Ambassador to the Holy See`
    `High Commissioner to Singapore`
    `Ambassador to Japan`
    `Ambassador and Permanent Representative to the OECD`
    `Ambassador to Italy`
    `High Commissioner to Canada`
    `Ambassador to Belgium`
    `Ambassador and Permanent Representative to the United Nations` HAS `post` IS A STRING
    `another office of the Commonwealth` HAS
        `the office is in a country or place outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the office is prescribed by the rules`                 IS A BOOLEAN
        `the office is that of a Head of Mission`               IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 7(1): "A designated diplomatic office is any of the following offices of the Commonwealth:
-- (a) the office of Ambassador to the United States of America; (b) any office of
-- Consul-General in the United States of America; (c) ... High Commissioner to the United
-- Kingdom; (d) ... High Commissioner to New Zealand; (e) ... Ambassador to Ireland; (f) ...
-- Ambassador to the Netherlands; (g) ... High Commissioner to India; (h) ... Ambassador to the
-- Holy See; (i) ... High Commissioner to Singapore; (j) ... Ambassador to Japan; (k) ...
-- Ambassador and Permanent Representative to the Organisation for Economic Cooperation and
-- Development; (l) ... Ambassador to Italy; (m) ... High Commissioner to Canada; (n) ...
-- Ambassador to Belgium; (o) any office of Ambassador and Permanent Representative to the
-- United Nations."
-- s 7(2): "An office of the Commonwealth in a country or place outside Australia is also a
-- designated diplomatic office if the office is prescribed by the rules."
-- No rules have been made; whether an office is prescribed is a fact (REF-06, REF-07).
@ref s 7(1), (2)
GIVEN o IS AN Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a designated diplomatic office` o IF
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `another office of the Commonwealth` outside prescribed head THEN outside AND prescribed
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Whether the office is that of the head of an Australian diplomatic or consular mission, which
-- the Public Service Act 1999 s 39 reads (psa-1999-s39.l4). Each office in s 7(1) heads a mission
-- (an embassy, high commission, consulate-general or permanent mission); an office prescribed
-- under s 7(2) may or may not (ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-10).
@ref s 7; Public Service Act 1999 s 7 'Head of Mission'
GIVEN o IS AN Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the office of a Head of Mission` o IF
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `another office of the Commonwealth` outside prescribed head THEN head
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `8 Political affiliations relevant to diplomatic appointments`

-- The facts s 8 reads about a person. Each is dated, because s 8 is asked "on" a day: the day of
-- an appointment (s 9(1)(a)), of a candidate list (s 10(2)) or of an acting arrangement (s 11(2)).
-- A day number of membership or employment is the first or last whole day of it.

DECLARE Legislature IS ONE OF
    `the Parliament of the Commonwealth`
    `the Parliament of a State`
    `the legislature of a Territory`
    `another body`

DECLARE Membership HAS
    `of`              IS A Legislature
    `began on`        IS A NUMBER
    `ended on`        IS A NUMBER
    `still a member`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- Employment under the MOP(S) Act 1984 (s 8(2)(b)): its kind, every position the employing
-- individual occupied while the person was so employed, and whether a determination under
-- MOP(S) Act s 4 was in force for the employing individual.
DECLARE `MOP(S) Act engagement` HAS
    `as`                                                   IS A `MOP(S) Act employment`
    `began on`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `a section 4 determination was in force for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `positions the employer occupied during the employment` IS A LIST OF Position

-- Employment under a State or Territory law (s 8(2)(c)). Whether the employer's position
-- "is equivalent or corresponds to" one in s 8(2)(b)(i)-(vi) is a fact: eight jurisdictions'
-- laws are out of scope (lqa.json scope; REF-14).
DECLARE `State or Territory staff engagement` HAS
    `began on`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `the employer's position corresponds to one in s 8(2)(b)(i) to (vi)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Being an officer or employee of a political party (s 8(2)(d)). Whether the party was, or is,
-- registered under Part XI of the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 is read from the Register
-- (REF-15); "officer or employee" is undefined and taken as a fact.
DECLARE `party role` HAS
    `began on`                                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the party was a registered political party while the role was held` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party is a registered political party on the day in question`   IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Person HAS
    `name`                                   IS A STRING
    `memberships`                            IS A LIST OF Membership
    `MOP(S) Act engagements`                 IS A LIST OF `MOP(S) Act engagement`
    `State or Territory staff engagements`   IS A LIST OF `State or Territory staff engagement`
    `party roles`                            IS A LIST OF `party role`
    `is an APS employee`                     IS A BOOLEAN

§§§ `The legislatures s 8 names`

-- s 8(1), (2)(a): "a member of the Parliament of the Commonwealth, the Parliament of a State or
-- the legislature of a Territory".
@ref s 8(1), (2)(a)
GIVEN l IS A Legislature
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a legislature s 8 names` l IF
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN `another body` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§§ `The last 10 years`

-- s 8(1) "at any time within the last 10 years"; s 8(2)(a) "at any time other than within the last
-- 10 years". The Bill does not say when the 10 years end; the encoding asks it on a day r (the day
-- of the appointment, list or arrangement) and the 10 years end at the end of r.
-- FORK-01, reading A (taken): the last 10 years is the period of 10 years ending at the end of day
-- r, which by analogy with Acts Interpretation Act s 2G(2) (120 months) begins at the start of the
-- day 10 years before the day after r. A membership that ended on the date exactly 10 years before
-- r ended before that period began.
@ref s 8(1), (2)(a); Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2G(2) by analogy
GIVEN r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first day of the last 10 years ending on` r MEANS
    `the same date` 10 `years before` (r PLUS 1)

-- FORK-01, reading B: the last 10 years also takes in the day exactly 10 years before r (the
-- anniversary), counted inclusively.
@ref s 8(1), (2)(a)
GIVEN r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first day of the last 10 years, reading B, ending on` r MEANS
    `the first day of the last 10 years ending on` r MINUS 1

-- A membership of a named legislature that was held on some day from s to r inclusive.
GIVEN m IS A Membership, s IS A NUMBER, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `membership` m `was held on some day from` s `to` r IF
        `is a legislature s 8 names` (m's `of`)
    AND m's `began on` AT MOST r
    AND (m's `still a member` OR m's `ended on` AT LEAST s)

GIVEN ms IS A LIST OF Membership
      s  IS A NUMBER
      r  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some membership in` ms `was held on some day from` s `to` r MEANS
    CONSIDER ms
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN m FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `membership` m `was held on some day from` s `to` r
     OR `some membership in` rest `was held on some day from` s `to` r

-- A membership of a named legislature that began before day s.
GIVEN ms IS A LIST OF Membership
      s  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some membership in` ms `began before` s MEANS
    CONSIDER ms
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN m FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (`is a legislature s 8 names` (m's `of`) AND m's `began on` LESS THAN s)
     OR `some membership in` rest `began before` s

§§§ `8(1) Disqualifying political affiliation`

-- s 8(1): "A person has a disqualifying political affiliation if the person is, or has been at
-- any time within the last 10 years, a member of the Parliament of the Commonwealth, the
-- Parliament of a State or the legislature of a Territory."
@ref s 8(1)
GIVEN p IS A Person, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` p r IF
    `some membership in` (p's `memberships`) `was held on some day from` (`the first day of the last 10 years ending on` r) `to` r

-- FORK-01, reading B.
@ref s 8(1)
GIVEN p IS A Person, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a disqualifying political affiliation, reading B, on` p r IF
    `some membership in` (p's `memberships`) `was held on some day from` (`the first day of the last 10 years, reading B, ending on` r) `to` r

§§§ `8(2) Significant political affiliation`

-- s 8(2)(a): "the person has been, at any time other than within the last 10 years, a member of
-- the Parliament of the Commonwealth, the Parliament of a State or the legislature of a
-- Territory".
@ref s 8(2)(a)
GIVEN p IS A Person, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 8(2)(a) applies to` p `on` r IF
    `some membership in` (p's `memberships`) `began before` (`the first day of the last 10 years ending on` r)

-- FORK-01, reading B.
@ref s 8(2)(a)
GIVEN p IS A Person, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 8(2)(a) applies to` p `on` r `, reading B` IF
    `some membership in` (p's `memberships`) `began before` (`the first day of the last 10 years, reading B, ending on` r)

-- s 8(2)(b): "the person is or has been employed under the Members of Parliament (Staff) Act 1984
-- as a member of the staff of a person occupying any of the following positions: (i) a Minister
-- (including the Prime Minister); (ii) the Leader of the Opposition in the Senate; (iii) the
-- Leader of the Opposition in the House of Representatives; (iv) the Deputy Leader of the
-- Opposition in the Senate; (v) the Deputy Leader of the Opposition in the House of
-- Representatives; (vi) a shadow Minister".
@ref s 8(2)(b)(i)-(vi)
GIVEN pos IS A Position
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a position listed in s 8(2)(b)` pos IF
    CONSIDER pos
    WHEN `Prime Minister` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Minister other than the Prime Minister` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Leader of the Opposition in the Senate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Leader of the Opposition in the House of Representatives` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Deputy Leader of the Opposition in the Senate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Deputy Leader of the Opposition in the House of Representatives` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `shadow Minister` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN k IS A `MOP(S) Act employment`, det IS A BOOLEAN, ps IS A LIST OF Position
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the engagement as` k `with a determination` det `is authorised for one of` ps MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN pos FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `employment as` k `by a person occupying` pos `with a section 4 determination in force` det `is authorised by section 11`
     OR `the engagement as` k `with a determination` det `is authorised for one of` rest

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF Position
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a position listed in s 8(2)(b) is among` ps MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN pos FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `is a position listed in s 8(2)(b)` pos OR `a position listed in s 8(2)(b) is among` rest

-- FORK-02, reading A (taken): "employed under the [MOP(S) Act] as a member of the staff of a person
-- occupying" a listed position covers any employment under the MOP(S) Act (s 11(1), (2) or (3))
-- by an employing individual who occupied a listed position while the person was so employed,
-- electorate employees included. The engagement must be one MOP(S) Act s 11 authorises.
@ref s 8(2)(b); MOP(S) Act 1984 ss 3, 3AA, 11
GIVEN e IS A `MOP(S) Act engagement`, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the engagement` e `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r IF
        e's `began on` AT MOST r
    AND `the engagement as` (e's `as`) `with a determination` (e's `a section 4 determination was in force for the employer`) `is authorised for one of` (e's `positions the employer occupied during the employment`)
    AND `a position listed in s 8(2)(b) is among` (e's `positions the employer occupied during the employment`)

-- FORK-02, reading B: only staff employed in the employer's capacity as holder of the position
-- count, that is personal employees (Ministerial or non-Ministerial), not electorate employees.
@ref s 8(2)(b); MOP(S) Act 1984 s 11
GIVEN e IS A `MOP(S) Act engagement`, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the engagement` e `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r `, reading B` IF
        `the engagement` e `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r
    AND (CONSIDER e's `as`
         WHEN `electorate employee` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `MOP(S) Act engagement`
      r  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some engagement in` es `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r MEANS
    CONSIDER es
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `the engagement` e `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r OR `some engagement in` rest `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r

GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `MOP(S) Act engagement`
      r  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some engagement in` es `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r `, reading B` MEANS
    CONSIDER es
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `the engagement` e `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r `, reading B` OR `some engagement in` rest `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r `, reading B`

-- s 8(2)(c): "the person is or has been employed under a law of a State or Territory as a member
-- of the staff of a person occupying a position in the State or Territory that is equivalent or
-- corresponds to a position mentioned in any of paragraphs (b)(i) to (vi)".
GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `State or Territory staff engagement`
      r  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some State or Territory engagement in` es `meets s 8(2)(c) by` r MEANS
    CONSIDER es
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (e's `began on` AT MOST r AND e's `the employer's position corresponds to one in s 8(2)(b)(i) to (vi)`)
     OR `some State or Territory engagement in` rest `meets s 8(2)(c) by` r

-- s 8(2)(d): "the person is or has been an officer or employee of a registered political party
-- (within the meaning of the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918)".
-- FORK-03, reading A (taken): the party must have been a registered political party (registered
-- under Part XI of that Act, s 4(1)) while the person held the role.
GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF `party role`
      r  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some party role in` rs `meets s 8(2)(d) by` r MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (x's `began on` AT MOST r AND x's `the party was a registered political party while the role was held`)
     OR `some party role in` rest `meets s 8(2)(d) by` r

-- FORK-03, reading B: the party must be a registered political party on the day the question is
-- asked, whether or not it was registered while the person held the role.
GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF `party role`
      r  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some party role in` rs `meets s 8(2)(d) by` r `, reading B` MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (x's `began on` AT MOST r AND x's `the party is a registered political party on the day in question`)
     OR `some party role in` rest `meets s 8(2)(d) by` r `, reading B`

-- s 8(2): "A person has a significant political affiliation if: (a) ...; or (b) ...; or (c) ...;
-- or (d) ...". The paragraphs are alternatives.
@ref s 8(2)
GIVEN p IS A Person, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a significant political affiliation on` p r IF
        `paragraph 8(2)(a) applies to` p `on` r
     OR `some engagement in` (p's `MOP(S) Act engagements`) `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r
     OR `some State or Territory engagement in` (p's `State or Territory staff engagements`) `meets s 8(2)(c) by` r
     OR `some party role in` (p's `party roles`) `meets s 8(2)(d) by` r

-- s 8(2) with FORK-02 reading B for paragraph (b).
@ref s 8(2)
GIVEN p IS A Person, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a significant political affiliation, reading B of FORK-02, on` p r IF
        `paragraph 8(2)(a) applies to` p `on` r
     OR `some engagement in` (p's `MOP(S) Act engagements`) `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r `, reading B`
     OR `some State or Territory engagement in` (p's `State or Territory staff engagements`) `meets s 8(2)(c) by` r
     OR `some party role in` (p's `party roles`) `meets s 8(2)(d) by` r

-- s 8(2) with FORK-03 reading B for paragraph (d).
@ref s 8(2)
GIVEN p IS A Person, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a significant political affiliation, reading B of FORK-03, on` p r IF
        `paragraph 8(2)(a) applies to` p `on` r
     OR `some engagement in` (p's `MOP(S) Act engagements`) `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r
     OR `some State or Territory engagement in` (p's `State or Territory staff engagements`) `meets s 8(2)(c) by` r
     OR `some party role in` (p's `party roles`) `meets s 8(2)(d) by` r `, reading B`

-- s 8(2) with FORK-01 reading B for paragraph (a).
@ref s 8(2)
GIVEN p IS A Person, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a significant political affiliation, reading B of FORK-01, on` p r IF
        `paragraph 8(2)(a) applies to` p `on` r `, reading B`
     OR `some engagement in` (p's `MOP(S) Act engagements`) `meets s 8(2)(b) by` r
     OR `some State or Territory engagement in` (p's `State or Territory staff engagements`) `meets s 8(2)(c) by` r
     OR `some party role in` (p's `party roles`) `meets s 8(2)(d) by` r
